[00:00.18] There we sat,
[00:02.96] In fluorescent haloes,
[00:07.06] The tiny flowering redemptions
[00:09.68] Of sharecroppers and miners and slaves,
[00:14.14] Offering up to our class,
[00:16.88] Beneath the TV, the flag and the cross,
[00:21.70] Our ridge-and-valley twangs and drawls,
[00:24.32] Birthmarks to be scrubbed away.
[00:28.60] I don't want to be a whitewash.
[00:32.66] I don't want to be an absence.
[00:35.82] I don't want to be the great silence.
[00:39.92] I want to be—
[00:43.22] I don't want to be a whitewash.
[00:47.28] I don't want to be nobody.
[00:50.98] I don't want to be from noplace.
[00:54.52] I want to be—
[00:58.20] In that little formica nook,
[01:01.10] Ladies at the steamtable, men from the scrapyard,
[01:05.34] Curling wisps from cornbread and collards,
[01:08.44] The soul of home, of souls forced west.
[01:12.70] The landlord will sell Ms. Glen's lease
[01:15.42] To continental cafes and unblinking empire,
[01:20.14] Pulling this scrap of red clay from those who
[01:22.78] Loved her through the worst, who loved her best.
[01:27.82] I don't want to be a whitewash.
[01:31.52] Don't want to wipe out memory.
[01:34.98] Don't want to fortify a colony.
[01:38.22] I want to be—
[01:41.44] I don't want to be a whitewash.
[01:45.78] Don't want power over anybody.
[01:49.38] Don't want dominion over anyplace.
[01:53.06] I want to be—
[01:57.80] Floating above
[02:01.26] Your scrapped-together smoker,
[02:05.62] In that hazy little yard
[02:08.72] On the sleepy Eastside,
[02:14.40] Smiling through blue strands of smoke
[02:17.40] At everybody passing—
[02:20.36] You're singing,
[02:22.12] As if
[02:22.90] Heaven
[02:24.38] Is
[02:24.64] Other folks.
[02:27.02] You might could sell them a book,
[02:29.40] Set in the boutiques of some blanched borough,
[02:34.24] In the sterile, phantom code of the mobile, modern,
[02:37.42] Skinny, shiny, and guilt-free.
[02:41.18] But you belong to the Free State of Winston.
[02:43.96] Her pines creak in your words, high and lonesome:
[02:48.30] "I've got a people, and a history,
[02:51.32] And a place bearing down on me."
[02:55.62] I don't want to be a whitewash,
[02:58.68] Turning places into sets,
[03:02.46] Turning people into objects.
[03:06.04] I want to be—
[03:09.20] I don't want to be a whitewash.
[03:12.90] Don't want power over anybody.
[03:16.32] Don't want dominion over anyplace.
[03:19.84] I want to be—
[03:23.02] I don't want to be a whitewash.
[03:28.10] I don't want to be a whitewash.
[03:37.18] I don't want to be a whitewash.
[03:42.04] I don't want to be a whitewash.
